---
const examples = [
  {
    you: "Spawn three agents in parallel: tests running pytest -x --ff, lint running ruff + pyright, format running ruff format. Notify me when any of them fail.",
    yields: "spawn_agent × 3 · child rows in AgentTable · roll-up totals to StatusBar",
  },
  {
    you: "Open a Review tab: orchestrator on top at 40%, below it a FileTree (30%) next to a DiffViewer (70%) showing the staged diff. Save it as review.",
    yields: "add_tab · set_layout · save_layout — applies atomically, rolls back on failure",
  },
  {
    you: "Build a custom TokenChart widget that draws my token usage over the last hour as a sparkline, and put it as a 25% sidebar on the right.",
    yields: "set_layout with custom_widgets — Python source ships at runtime, isolated namespace",
  },
];
---

<section id="examples" class="py-20 sm:py-28">
  <div class="container-page">
    <div class="reveal max-w-2xl">
      <p class="mono text-sm text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">/* it's conversational */</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-4xl">
        Each of these is one message.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)]">
        The orchestrator owns the spec; you own the ideas. Every command below routes through a
        structured tool call — <code class="mono text-[color:var(--color-fg)]">spawn_agent</code>,
        <code class="mono text-[color:var(--color-fg)]">set_layout</code>,
        <code class="mono text-[color:var(--color-fg)]">save_layout</code>,
        <code class="mono text-[color:var(--color-fg)]">bind_key</code> — applied atomically with
        rollback on failure.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-5">
      {
        examples.map((ex, i) => (
          <div
            class="reveal rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-bg-card)] p-5 sm:p-6"
            style={`transition-delay: ${i * 60}ms`}
          >
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="mono mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">&gt;</span>
              <p class="mono text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-fg)] sm:text-base">
                {ex.you}
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-4 flex items-start gap-3 border-t border-dashed border-[var(--color-border)] pt-4">
              <span class="mono mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-[color:var(--color-fg-dim)]">↳</span>
              <p class="mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)] sm:text-sm">
                {ex.yields}
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <div class="reveal mt-10 rounded-xl border border-dashed border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-bg-soft)] p-5 sm:p-6">
      <p class="mono text-sm text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)]">
        <span class="text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">[migrator → orchestrator]</span>
        (asking) Should I bump min Python to 3.11 or stay on 3.10?
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)]">
        Children get
        <code class="mono text-[color:var(--color-fg)]">notify_orchestrator</code>
        and
        <code class="mono text-[color:var(--color-fg)]">ask_orchestrator</code>
        injected automatically. A migration agent can stop and ask — you answer through
        the orchestrator and the reply becomes the tool result on the child's side.
        No modal. No context switch.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
